otin E_R$, $d_i^r < d_i$, and $d_j^r < d_j$. Then neither $G_S$ nor $G_{SU}$ are identified. [Proof, corrected: the starting graph is constructed, so that $\{i, j\}$ is absent from it (P012-E003), and the two recruitment-induced subgraphs are compatible in the sense defined at the opening of the proof (P012-N005)] Call a recruitment-induced subgraph $G_S = (V_S, E_S)$ compatible with the observed data if $V_S = V_R$, $\{i, j\} \in E_R$ implies $\{i, j\} \in E_S$, and $\sum_{j 
